		bodyHtml: `<p>Mercy is <strong>compassion in action toward someone in need or in the wrong</strong>. It withholds the punishment deserved and moves to help. In Scripture it flows from our Father&rsquo;s own nature: &ldquo;Our Father is compassionate and gracious, slow to anger and abounding in covenant love&rdquo; (Psalm 103:8).</p><p>And it never runs out: &ldquo;The covenant love of our Father never ceases; his mercies never come to an end; they are new every morning; great is your faithfulness&rdquo; (Lamentations 3:22&ndash;23).</p>`,
